# Cline Custom Rules - Vibe Coding Mode

## General Behavior
- Read before writing: Always read existing files before editing
- Test your code: Run relevant tests after making changes
- Explain simply: Comment complex logic, but don't over-comment obvious code
- Before making structural changes (renaming folders, moving files, or changing project architecture), ask for confirmation

## Project Structure
- Follow existing patterns in the codebase
- Don't create files outside the project without asking
- Use TypeScript/JavaScript consistently (no mixing styles)

## Safety
- NEVER run destructive commands without confirmation (rm -rf, git reset --hard, drop table)
- Check git status before committing
- Ask before installing new npm dependencies for production

## Context Management
- Use `read_file` only on necessary files — don't read entire codebase upfront
- Summarize changes and current state at the end of each task to manage context efficiently

## Environment & Standards
- Strictly follow the project's linting and formatting rules (e.g., ESLint, Prettier). Auto-fix any lint errors before requesting review.
- For JavaScript/TypeScript projects, use only the module syntax already established in the codebase (CommonJS or ESM). Do not mix them.

## Package Management
- After modifying `package.json`, run the package manager that matches the existing lockfile (`npm install`, `yarn install`, or `pnpm install`). Never update `package.json` without also updating the lockfile.

## Git Commit Strategy
- Write concise, conventional commits (e.g., `feat: add login button`, `fix: resolve API crash`). Reject blank or generic messages like "changes made".

## Vibe Coding Specific
- Focus on getting things done, not perfection
- Build in small chunks and verify as you go
- Don't over-engineer solutions
- Keep context minimal - compact when context gets large
- Prioritize working code over perfect code

## Cell'EX Project Context & Memory Bank (CRITICAL)
- Project Identity: Proyek ini adalah web direktori layanan digital dan teknis bernama "Cell'EX".
- Design Rules: Wajib menggunakan estetika "Dark Tech Minimalist". DILARANG menggunakan gaya template AI generik (seperti biru tech, gradien ungu, drop-shadow tebal, atau border sangat membulat).
- Memory Bank: SEBELUM mengeksekusi tugas atau membuat komponen baru, kamu WAJIB membaca dan menerapkan referensi dari docs/design-system.md, docs/tech-stack.md, dan docs/project-brief.md.
- Execution: Jangan membuat asumsi desain sendiri. Selalu ikuti panduan palet warna dan tipografi monospace yang ada di Memory Bank.